{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/ws_project.cljc'","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns dao.stream.ws-project\n     2\t  \"The WebSocket channel composition of dao.stream.remote.md (3.1).\n     3\t\n     4\t   The mirror and the link of dao.stream.remote speak raw request and\n     5\t   answer maps, so each channel end composes one step, the projection,\n     6\t   between the ws deposit medium and the channel: the channel reader is\n     7\t   a ring buffer the composition wires, the channel writer is the ws\n     8\t   handle itself. The projection holds the reading cursor on the\n     9\t   attachment's traffic medium, keeps the events whose :ws/attachment\n    10\t   names this channel, appends the :ws/value of each :ws/payload onto\n    11\t   the ring, and drops :ws/error diagnostics. A terminal lifecycle\n    12\t   event (:ws/closed, :ws/ended) or a failure resolution (:ws/not-found,\n    13\t   :ws/transport-error) makes the projection close the ring: channel\n    14\t   loss is then the link's own end observation (2.4).\n    15\t\n    16\t   The composition helpers wire both ends of the spec's section-5 toy\n    17\t   over real attachments. The accepting peer drives `accept-step!`:\n    18\t   endpoint steps, one offer adopted per tick (a fresh traffic medium\n    19\t   and ring per accepted connection, acknowledged per dao.stream.ws.md\n    20\t   Serving), then per session the projection and, over the projected\n    21\t   reader and the socket handle, dao.stream.remote/mirror-step. The\n    22\t   dialing peer composes `dial` over one ws attacher and drives\n    23\t   `dial-step!`: the projection and then its own mirror step, so either\n    24\t   peer serves the other on one connection. Reflections come from\n    25\t   dao.stream.remote/attacher through the channel end each side holds.\n    26\t   Every step here is driver-paced: the composition owns the cadence,\n    27\t   as it does for endpoint-step. Nothing schedules itself.\"\n    28\t  (:require [dao.stream :as stream]\n    29\t            [dao.stream.remote :as remote]\n    30\t            [dao.stream.ws :as ws]))\n    31\t\n    32\t\n    33\t(def terminal-events\n    34\t  \"The deposited events that end the channel: a terminal lifecycle\n    35\t   event for the attachment (:ws/closed, :ws/ended) or a failure\n    36\t   resolution (:ws/not-found, :ws/transport-error). The projection\n    37\t   closes the ring on each of them. :ws/error is a diagnostic and is\n    38\t   never terminal by itself (dao.stream.ws.md, Deposited events are\n    39\t   envelopes).\"\n    40\t  #{:ws/closed :ws/ended :ws/not-found :ws/transport-error})\n    41\t\n    42\t\n    43\t;; =============================================================================\n    44\t;; The projection (3.1's ws-project step)\n    45\t;; =============================================================================\n    46\t\n    47\t(defn projection\n    48\t  \"Compose one projection over the attachment named `:attachment` (the\n    49\t   :ws/attachment value every deposited event of this channel carries),\n    50\t   the traffic medium reader `:traffic`, the already-minted reading\n    51\t   cursor `:cursor`, and the ring buffer `:ring` the channel reads.\n    52\t   The projection owns the cursor from here: each `step!` advances it.\"\n    53\t  [{:keys [attachment traffic cursor ring]}]\n    54\t  (when-not (and (some? attachment)\n    55\t                 (stream/reader? traffic)\n    56\t                 (some? cursor)\n    57\t                 (stream/reader? ring)\n    58\t                 (stream/writer? ring)\n    59\t                 (stream/closable? ring))\n    60\t    (throw (ex-info \"invalid DaoStream ws projection composition\"\n    61\t                    {:attachment attachment :traffic traffic\n    62\t                     :cursor cursor :ring ring})))\n    63\t  (atom {:attachment attachment :traffic traffic :cursor cursor\n    64\t         :ring ring :closed? false}))\n    65\t\n    66\t\n    67\t(defn- project!\n    68\t  \"Apply one deposited event (3.1): another attachment's event and\n    69\t   every non-payload, non-terminal kind are ignored here; a :ws/error\n    70\t   is dropped as a diagnostic; a :ws/payload's :ws/value is appended\n    71\t   onto the ring; a terminal event or failure resolution closes the\n    72\t   ring. True only for the terminal case.\"\n    73\t  [state event]\n    74\t  (when (= (:ws/attachment event) (:attachment state))\n    75\t    (let [kind (:ws/event event)]\n    76\t      (cond\n    77\t        (= :ws/payload kind)\n    78\t        (do (when (contains? event :ws/value)\n    79\t              (stream/append! (:ring state) (:ws/value event)))\n    80\t            nil)\n    81\t\n    82\t        (= :ws/error kind) nil\n    83\t\n    84\t        (contains? terminal-events kind)\n    85\t        (do (stream/close! (:ring state)) true)\n    86\t\n    87\t        :else nil))))\n    88\t\n    89\t\n    90\t(defn step!\n    91\t  \"Drive the projection once, at the composition's cadence: read the\n    92\t   traffic medium to blocked, keeping, forwarding and dropping per\n    93\t   3.1, stopping at the event that closes the ring. A gap adopts the\n    94\t   medium's own recovery cursor, the lost events being lost. The\n    95\t   medium's own end closes the projection -- the ring's fate stays\n    96\t   with the four deposited events the spec names. Returns the\n    97\t   projection.\"\n    98\t  [project]\n    99\t  (loop []\n   100\t    (let [s @project]\n   101\t      (if (:closed? s)\n   102\t        project\n   103\t        (let [r (stream/next (:traffic s) (:cursor s))]\n   104\t          (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n   105\t            :dao.stream/ok\n   106\t            (let [event (:dao.stream/value r)]\n   107\t              (swap! project assoc :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   108\t              (if (project! s event)\n   109\t                (swap! project assoc :closed? true)\n   110\t                (recur)))\n   111\t\n   112\t            :dao.stream/end\n   113\t            (do (swap! project assoc :closed? true) project)\n   114\t\n   115\t            :dao.stream/gap\n   116\t            (do (swap! project assoc :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   117\t                (recur))\n   118\t\n   119\t            ;; blocked, and any read the medium refuses: stay put.\n   120\t            project))))))\n   121\t\n   122\t\n   123\t(defn closed?\n   124\t  \"True once the projection stopped: the ring was closed by a terminal\n   125\t   lifecycle event or a failure resolution, or the traffic medium\n   126\t   itself answered end.\"\n   127\t  [project]\n   128\t  (:closed? @project))\n   129\t\n   130\t\n   131\t(defn reading-cursor\n   132\t  \"The projection's current reading cursor on the traffic medium.\"\n   133\t  [project]\n   134\t  (:cursor @project))\n   135\t\n   136\t\n   137\t;; =============================================================================\n   138\t;; The accepting peer (section 5: accept, project, mirror)\n   139\t;; =============================================================================\n   140\t\n   141\t(defn- writer-target?\n   142\t  [x]\n   143\t  (and (map? x)\n   144\t       (stream/writer? (:dao.stream/handle x))\n   145\t       (contains? (:dao.stream/surface x) :writer)))\n   146\t\n   147\t\n   148\t(defn- valid-slot?\n   149\t  [{:keys [offer-reader offer-cursor ack-writer]}]\n   150\t  (and (stream/reader? offer-reader)\n   151\t       (some? offer-cursor)\n   152\t       (writer-target? ack-writer)))\n   153\t\n   154\t\n   155\t(defn make-acceptor\n   156\t  \"Compose the accepting end of the spec's section-5 toy.\n   157\t   `:endpoint` is a dao.stream.ws/make-endpoint value whose handoff\n   158\t   `:slots` are given here, in endpoint order, as {:offer-reader r\n   159\t   :offer-cursor c :ack-writer target} -- readers, cursors and writers\n   160\t   the composition minted before the listener started. `:table` is the\n   161\t   mirror's table (dao.stream.remote.md 2.2). `:make-media` receives\n   162\t   one accepted offer and returns the attachment's composition:\n   163\t   :traffic (the deposit target the acknowledgement carries),\n   164\t   :admission (its declaration), :reader (the traffic reader the\n   165\t   projection reads), :cursor (its minted reading cursor) and :ring\n   166\t   (the fresh channel ring buffer). The listener is the host's: it\n   167\t   calls ws/accept-connection! on this endpoint, per dao.stream.ws.md\n   168\t   Serving.\"\n   169\t  [{:keys [endpoint slots table make-media] :as config}]\n   170\t  (when-not (and (map? config)\n   171\t                 (some? endpoint)\n   172\t                 (fn? make-media)\n   173\t                 (map? table)\n   174\t                 (seq slots)\n   175\t                 (every? valid-slot? slots))\n   176\t    (throw (ex-info \"invalid DaoStream ws acceptor composition\"\n   177\t                    {:config config})))\n   178\t  (atom {:endpoint endpoint\n   179\t         :slots (vec slots)\n   180\t         :table table\n   181\t         :make-media make-media\n   182\t         :offer-cursors (mapv :offer-cursor slots)\n   183\t         :sessions {}}))\n   184\t\n   185\t\n   186\t(defn- adopt!\n   187\t  \"Adopt one accepted offer as a session: create the attachment's\n   188\t   media through :make-media, acknowledge the offer per\n   189\t   dao.stream.ws.md Serving (:ws/command :ws/accept, the deposit\n   190\t   target and its admission), and register the projection, ring,\n   191\t   reading cursor and socket handle the mirror works through. An\n   192\t   offer that is not an acceptance, and an acknowledgement the slot's\n   193\t   medium refuses, close the offered handle; the slot itself is the\n   194\t   endpoint's to release.\"\n   195\t  [acceptor slot offer]\n   196\t  (let [make-media (:make-media @acceptor)\n   197\t        handle (get-in offer [:ws/handle :dao.stream/handle])\n   198\t        attachment (:ws/attachment offer)]\n   199\t    (if-not (and (= :ws/accepted (:ws/event offer))\n   200\t                 (string? attachment)\n   201\t                 (some? handle)\n   202\t                 (stream/writer? handle)\n   203\t                 (stream/closable? handle))\n   204\t      (when (stream/closable? handle)\n   205\t        (stream/close! handle))\n   206\t      (let [media (make-media offer)\n   207\t            appended (stream/append!\n   208\t                       (:dao.stream/handle (:ack-writer slot))\n   209\t                       {:ws/attachment attachment\n   210\t                        :ws/command :ws/accept\n   211\t                        :ws/deposit (:traffic media)\n   212\t                        :ws/admission (:admission media)})]\n   213\t        (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome appended))\n   214\t          (swap! acceptor assoc-in [:sessions attachment]\n   215\t                 {:attachment attachment\n   216\t                  :handle handle\n   217\t                  :ring (:ring media)\n   218\t                  :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor\n   219\t                            (stream/cursor (:ring media)\n   220\t                                           stream/anchor-oldest))\n   221\t                  :project (projection\n   222\t                             {:attachment attachment\n   223\t                              :traffic (:reader media)\n   224\t                              :cursor (:cursor media)\n   225\t                              :ring (:ring media)})})\n   226\t          (stream/close! handle))))))\n   227\t\n   228\t\n   229\t(defn accept-step!\n   230\t  \"Advance the accepting composition one tick at `now`, in the order\n   231\t   serving compositions use: a transport step first (releasing dead\n   232\t   pendings, consuming standing acknowledgements), then one offer per\n   233\t   slot adopted with its fresh media and acknowledgement, then a\n   234\t   second transport step, so the fresh acknowledgement is consumed and\n   235\t   the accept frame is on the wire before this end answers anything,\n   236\t   then per session the projection and, over the projected reader and\n   237\t   the socket handle, the mirror step. Returns the acceptor.\"\n   238\t  [acceptor now]\n   239\t  (let [{:keys [endpoint slots] :as s} @acceptor]\n   240\t    (ws/endpoint-step endpoint now)\n   241\t    (doseq [[index slot] (map-indexed vector slots)]\n   242\t      (let [r (stream/next (:offer-reader slot)\n   243\t                           (nth (:offer-cursors s) index))]\n   244\t        (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n   245\t          (swap! acceptor assoc-in [:offer-cursors index]\n   246\t                 (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   247\t          (adopt! acceptor slot (:dao.stream/value r)))))\n   248\t    (ws/endpoint-step endpoint now)\n   249\t    (doseq [[attachment session] (:sessions @acceptor)]\n   250\t      (step! (:project session))\n   251\t      (swap! acceptor assoc-in [:sessions attachment :cursor]\n   252\t             (remote/mirror-step (:table @acceptor)\n   253\t                                 (:ring session)\n   254\t                                 (:cursor session)\n   255\t                                 (:handle session))))\n   256\t    acceptor))\n   257\t\n   258\t\n   259\t(defn sessions\n   260\t  \"The acceptor's sessions as data: attachment id -> {:attachment\n   261\t   :handle :ring :cursor :project}.\"\n   262\t  [acceptor]\n   263\t  (:sessions @acceptor))\n   264\t\n   265\t\n   266\t(defn session-end\n   267\t  \"One accepted attachment's channel end {:reader r :writer w} -- the\n   268\t   ring this end projects onto and the socket handle it writes\n   269\t   through: the entry for dao.stream.remote/attacher's\n   270\t   :dao.stream.remote/channels map at this end, so the accepting peer\n   271\t   can attach reflections of the other direction over the same\n   272\t   connection. Nil before the attachment is adopted.\"\n   273\t  [acceptor attachment]\n   274\t  (when-some [session (get (:sessions @acceptor) attachment)]\n   275\t    {:reader (:ring session) :writer (:handle session)}))\n   276\t\n   277\t\n   278\t;; =============================================================================\n   279\t;; The dialing peer (section 5: the link over its dialed attachment)\n   280\t;; =============================================================================\n   281\t\n   282\t(defn dial\n   283\t  \"Compose the dialing end of one WebSocket channel (3.1). `:attach!`\n   284\t   is the dao.stream.ws/make-attacher product whose :traffic deposit\n   285\t   medium is the same medium named by `:traffic` (its target), with\n   286\t   `:cursor` already minted on it before any attach!; `:ring` is the\n   287\t   channel ring buffer this end projects onto. `:table` names the\n   288\t   identities this peer serves over the dialed channel, so\n   289\t   `dial-step!` runs the projection and then this end's own mirror\n   290\t   step: the dialing end serves the other direction on the same\n   291\t   connection. `dial-attach!` takes a remote descriptor whose\n   292\t   :dao.stream/channel is this channel's ws descriptor: it attaches,\n   293\t   projects the attachment onto the ring, and answers through\n   294\t   dao.stream.remote/attacher with the channel end {:reader ring\n   295\t   :writer handle} -- the link's drain then runs inside every\n   296\t   reflection operation. One dial value carries one active\n   297\t   attachment; a reattachment composes a fresh dial with a fresh\n   298\t   cursor, as dao.stream.ws.md composes one medium per active client\n   299\t   attachment. :dao.stream.remote/events, :dao.stream.remote/resend-\n   300\t   after and :dao.stream.remote/budget pass to the attacher as its\n   301\t   policy.\"\n   302\t  [{:keys [attach! traffic cursor ring table] :as opts}]\n   303\t  (when-not (and (fn? attach!)\n   304\t                 (map? traffic)\n   305\t                 (stream/writer? (:dao.stream/handle traffic))\n   306\t                 (stream/reader? (:dao.stream/handle traffic))\n   307\t                 (some? cursor)\n   308\t                 (stream/reader? ring)\n   309\t                 (stream/writer? ring)\n   310\t                 (stream/closable? ring)\n   311\t                 (map? table))\n   312\t    (throw (ex-info \"invalid DaoStream ws dial composition\"\n   313\t                    {:opts opts})))\n   314\t  (let [channel (atom nil)\n   315\t        mirror-cursor (atom (:dao.stream/cursor\n   316\t                              (stream/cursor ring stream/anchor-oldest)))\n   317\t        policy (select-keys opts [:dao.stream.remote/events\n   318\t                                  :dao.stream.remote/resend-after\n   319\t                                  :dao.stream.remote/budget])]\n   320\t    (atom {:attach! attach! :traffic traffic :cursor cursor :ring ring\n   321\t           :table table :channel channel :mirror-cursor mirror-cursor\n   322\t           :policy policy})))\n   323\t\n   324\t\n   325\t(defn dial-attach!\n   326\t  \"Attach one reflection of `descriptor` (a :dao.stream/remote\n   327\t   descriptor) through the dialed channel: the ws attach runs first,\n   328\t   the attachment's projection is composed, and the remote attacher\n   329\t   answers with the reflection -- its confirmation deferred, per\n   330\t   dao.stream.remote.md 2.4, to the descriptor probe the link sends\n   331\t   now. A channel attach that fails answers the ws attacher's own\n   332\t   outcome. Returns the remote attach! result.\"\n   333\t  [dial descriptor]\n   334\t  (let [{:keys [attach! traffic cursor ring channel policy]} @dial\n   335\t        r (attach! (:dao.stream/channel descriptor))]\n   336\t    (if-not (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n   337\t      r\n   338\t      (let [cd (:dao.stream/channel descriptor)\n   339\t            handle (:dao.stream/handle r)\n   340\t            project (projection {:attachment (:dao.stream/attachment r)\n   341\t                                 :traffic (:dao.stream/handle traffic)\n   342\t                                 :cursor cursor\n   343\t                                 :ring ring})\n   344\t            reflect! (remote/attacher\n   345\t                       (merge policy\n   346\t                              {:dao.stream.remote/channels\n   347\t                               {cd {:reader ring :writer handle}}}))]\n   348\t        (reset! channel {:attachment (:dao.stream/attachment r)\n   349\t                         :handle handle :project project})\n   350\t        (reflect! descriptor)))))\n   351\t\n   352\t\n   353\t(defn dial-step!\n   354\t  \"Drive the dialing composition one tick, at the composition's\n   355\t   cadence: the attachment's projection first, so what the wire\n   356\t   deposited reaches the ring, then this end's own mirror step over\n   357\t   the projected reader and the socket handle, answering the other\n   358\t   direction's requests against this end's table. Returns the\n   359\t   mirror's advanced reading cursor.\"\n   360\t  [dial]\n   361\t  (let [{:keys [ring table channel mirror-cursor]} @dial]\n   362\t    (when-some [project (:project @channel)]\n   363\t      (step! project))\n   364\t    (when-some [handle (:handle @channel)]\n   365\t      (swap! mirror-cursor\n   366\t             (fn [c] (remote/mirror-step table ring c handle))))\n   367\t    @mirror-cursor))\n   368\t\n   369\t\n   370\t(defn channel\n   371\t  \"The dialed channel as data: {:attachment id :handle h :project p} --\n   372\t   the ws attachment identity, the ws handle (the channel writer), and\n   373\t   the attachment's projection. Nil before the first dial-attach!. A\n   374\t   composition that owns the connection's lifetime closes the handle\n   375\t   here.\"\n   376\t  [dial]\n   377\t  @(:channel @dial))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba test/dao/stream/ws_project_test.cljc; nl -ba test/dao/stream/ws_project_jvm_test.clj'","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns dao.stream.ws-project-test\n     2\t  \"The projection (dao.stream.remote.md 3.1's ws-project step) as a\n     3\t   unit: value forwarding onto the ring, :ws/attachment filtering,\n     4\t   :ws/error diagnostics dropped, cursor keeping across steps, a gap\n     5\t   adopting the medium's recovery cursor, and the four terminal and\n     6\t   failure-resolution events closing the ring -- channel loss then\n     7\t   being the link's own end observation.\"\n     8\t  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n     9\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    10\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]\n    11\t            [dao.stream.ws-project :as project]))\n    12\t\n    13\t\n    14\t(def ^:private me \"att-1\")\n    15\t\n    16\t\n    17\t(defn- ring\n    18\t  [capacity]\n    19\t  (:dao.stream/handle\n    20\t    (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type ringbuffer/transport-type\n    21\t                         ringbuffer/capacity-key capacity})))\n    22\t\n    23\t\n    24\t(defn- payload\n    25\t  [attachment v]\n    26\t  {:ws/attachment attachment :ws/event :ws/payload :ws/value v})\n    27\t\n    28\t\n    29\t(defn- event\n    30\t  [attachment kind]\n    31\t  {:ws/attachment attachment :ws/event kind})\n    32\t\n    33\t\n    34\t(defn- deposit!\n    35\t  \"Deposit one envelope onto the traffic medium, as the host adapter\n    36\t   would.\"\n    37\t  [medium envelope]\n    38\t  (stream/append! medium envelope))\n    39\t\n    40\t\n    41\t(defn- composed\n    42\t  \"A projection over a fresh traffic medium and channel ring, both\n    43\t   capacity `cap`, with the reading cursor minted before anything is\n    44\t   deposited -- the composition discipline of dao.stream.ws.md.\"\n    45\t  ([cap]\n    46\t   (let [medium (ring cap)\n    47\t         channel (ring cap)\n    48\t         cursor (:dao.stream/cursor\n    49\t                  (stream/cursor medium stream/anchor-newest))]\n    50\t     {:medium medium\n    51\t      :channel channel\n    52\t      :project (project/projection {:attachment me\n    53\t                                    :traffic medium\n    54\t                                    :cursor cursor\n    55\t                                    :ring channel})}))\n    56\t  ([] (composed 64)))\n    57\t\n    58\t\n    59\t(defn- read-all\n    60\t  \"Every retained read of `h`, oldest first, as raw outcome maps, so a\n    61\t   test can tell a read of nil from no read.\"\n    62\t  [h]\n    63\t  (loop [c (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor h stream/anchor-oldest))\n    64\t         acc []]\n    65\t    (let [r (stream/next h c)]\n    66\t      (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n    67\t        (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r) (conj acc r))\n    68\t        acc))))\n    69\t\n    70\t\n    71\t(defn- values\n    72\t  \"Every retained value of `h`, oldest first.\"\n    73\t  [h]\n    74\t  (mapv :dao.stream/value (read-all h)))\n    75\t\n    76\t\n    77\t(defn- newest-cursor\n    78\t  [h]\n    79\t  (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor h stream/anchor-newest)))\n    80\t\n    81\t\n    82\t(defn- blocked?\n    83\t  \"True while `h` reads blocked at its newest position: nothing new.\"\n    84\t  [h]\n    85\t  (let [newest (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor h stream/anchor-newest))]\n    86\t    (= :dao.stream/blocked (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/next h newest)))))\n    87\t\n    88\t\n    89\t(deftest forwards-each-payload-value-onto-the-ring-in-order\n    90\t  (let [{:keys [medium channel project]} (composed)]\n    91\t    (deposit! medium (payload me :a))\n    92\t    (deposit! medium (payload me \"two\"))\n    93\t    (deposit! medium (payload me nil))\n    94\t    (project/step! project)\n    95\t    (is (= [:a \"two\" nil] (values channel))\n    96\t        \"one ring value per payload, in deposit order\")\n    97\t    (let [third (last (read-all channel))]\n    98\t      (is (contains? third :dao.stream/value))\n    99\t      (is (nil? (:dao.stream/value third))\n   100\t          \"nil rides as a value: the event carries :ws/value, so nil\n   101\t           is forwarded, not dropped\"))\n   102\t    (is (not (project/closed? project))\n   103\t        \"payloads are not terminal\")))\n   104\t\n   105\t\n   106\t(deftest keeps-only-the-events-of-this-channel\n   107\t  (let [{:keys [medium channel project]} (composed)]\n   108\t    (deposit! medium (payload \"att-2\" :foreign))\n   109\t    (deposit! medium (payload me :mine))\n   110\t    (deposit! medium (event \"att-2\" :ws/closed))\n   111\t    (deposit! medium (payload nil :orphan))\n   112\t    (project/step! project)\n   113\t    (is (= [:mine] (values channel))\n   114\t        \"another attachment's payloads and events, and an event with no\n   115\t         attachment at all, are not this channel's\")\n   116\t    (is (not (project/closed? project))\n   117\t        \"another attachment's terminal event does not end this channel\")))\n   118\t\n   119\t\n   120\t(deftest drops-error-diagnostics-and-keeps-projecting\n   121\t  (let [{:keys [medium channel project]} (composed)]\n   122\t    (deposit! medium (payload me :before))\n   123\t    (deposit! medium {:ws/attachment me :ws/event :ws/error\n   124\t                      :ws/reason :ws/decode-failure})\n   125\t    (deposit! medium (payload me :after))\n   126\t    (project/step! project)\n   127\t    (is (= [:before :after] (values channel))\n   128\t        \"the diagnostic appends nothing, its neighbours both forward\")\n   129\t    (is (not (project/closed? project))\n   130\t        \":ws/error is never terminal by itself\")\n   131\t    (project/step! project)\n   132\t    (is (blocked? channel)\n   133\t        \"the cursor advanced past all three events: nothing re-reads\")))\n   134\t\n   135\t\n   136\t(deftest cursor-keeping-spans-steps-without-re-reading\n   137\t  (let [{:keys [medium channel project]} (composed)]\n   138\t    (deposit! medium (payload me :one))\n   139\t    (project/step! project)\n   140\t    (is (= [:one] (values channel)))\n   141\t    (deposit! medium (payload me :two))\n   142\t    (project/step! project)\n   143\t    (is (= [:one :two] (values channel))\n   144\t        \"each step reads forward from where the last stopped\")\n   145\t    (project/step! project)\n   146\t    (project/step! project)\n   147\t    (is (= [:one :two] (values channel))\n   148\t        \"a quiet medium advances nothing\")))\n   149\t\n   150\t\n   151\t(deftest payload-then-terminal-in-one-step-forward-then-close\n   152\t  (let [{:keys [medium channel project]} (composed)]\n   153\t    (deposit! medium (payload me :x))\n   154\t    (deposit! medium (event me :ws/closed))\n   155\t    (project/step! project)\n   156\t    (is (= [:x] (values channel))\n   157\t        \"the payload ahead of the terminal event still forwarded\")\n   158\t    (is (project/closed? project))\n   159\t    (is (= :dao.stream/end\n   160\t           (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/next channel (newest-cursor channel))))\n   161\t        \"the closed ring reads end at its tail: channel loss is the\n   162\t         link's observation (2.4)\")))\n   163\t\n   164\t\n   165\t(deftest terminal-lifecycle-events-close-the-ring\n   166\t  (doseq [kind [:ws/closed :ws/ended]]\n   167\t    (testing kind\n   168\t      (let [{:keys [medium channel project]} (composed)]\n   169\t        (deposit! medium (payload me :last))\n   170\t        (deposit! medium (event me kind))\n   171\t        (project/step! project)\n   172\t        (is (project/closed? project))\n   173\t        (is (= [:last] (values channel)))\n   174\t        (deposit! medium (payload me :late))\n   175\t        (project/step! project)\n   176\t        (is (= [:last] (values channel))\n   177\t            \"a step past the terminal event projects nothing: the\n   178\t             projection stopped on it\")\n   179\t        (is (= :dao.stream/closed\n   180\t               (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! channel :x)))\n   181\t            \"the ring refuses further appends\")))))\n   182\t\n   183\t\n   184\t(deftest failure-resolutions-close-the-ring\n   185\t  (doseq [kind [:ws/not-found :ws/transport-error]]\n   186\t    (testing kind\n   187\t      (let [{:keys [medium channel project]} (composed)]\n   188\t        (deposit! medium (payload me :before))\n   189\t        (deposit! medium (event me kind))\n   190\t        (project/step! project)\n   191\t        (is (project/closed? project))\n   192\t        (is (= [:before] (values channel)))\n   193\t        (is (= :dao.stream/end\n   194\t               (:dao.stream/outcome\n   195\t                 (stream/next channel (newest-cursor channel)))))))))\n   196\t\n   197\t\n   198\t(deftest resolution-and-other-kinds-are-not-payload\n   199\t  (let [{:keys [medium channel project]} (composed)]\n   200\t    (deposit! medium (event me :ws/opened))\n   201\t    (deposit! medium {:ws/attachment me :ws/event :ws/accepted\n   202\t                      :ws/handle {:dao.stream/handle (ring 1)\n   203\t                                  :dao.stream/surface #{:writer}}})\n   204\t    (deposit! medium {:ws/attachment me :ws/event :ws/payload})\n   205\t    (project/step! project)\n   206\t    (is (= [] (values channel))\n   207\t        \"openings, offers and a payload without :ws/value append\n   208\t         nothing\")\n   209\t    (is (not (project/closed? project))\n   210\t        \"none of them is terminal\")))\n   211\t\n   212\t\n   213\t(deftest a-gap-adopts-the-mediums-recovery-cursor\n   214\t  (let [{:keys [medium channel project]} (composed 1)]\n   215\t    (deposit! medium (payload me :lost))\n   216\t    (deposit! medium (payload me :kept))\n   217\t    (project/step! project)\n   218\t    (is (= [:kept] (values channel))\n   219\t        \"the evicted event is lost, the retained one forwards\")\n   220\t    (is (not (project/closed? project))\n   221\t        \"a medium gap is not channel loss\")))\n   222\t\n   223\t\n   224\t(deftest the-mediums-own-end-closes-the-projection-not-the-ring\n   225\t  (let [{:keys [medium channel project]} (composed)]\n   226\t    (deposit! medium (payload me :only))\n   227\t    (stream/close! medium)\n   228\t    (project/step! project)\n   229\t    (is (= [:only] (values channel))\n   230\t        \"what the medium retained before it ended still forwards\")\n   231\t    (is (project/closed? project)\n   232\t        \"a dead medium gives the projection nothing further to read\")\n   233\t    (is (blocked? channel)\n   234\t        \"the four deposited events close the ring; the medium's fate\n   235\t         does not (minimal reading of 3.1)\")))\n     1\t(ns dao.stream.ws-project-jvm-test\n     2\t  \"The section-5 toy of dao.stream.remote.md across a real socket.\n     3\t\n     4\t   Peer B serves the single value \\\"hello\\\" as \\\"str-1\\\" behind a real\n     5\t   http-kit listener and drives, per accepted connection, the\n     6\t   projection and then the mirror step. Peer A dials through the real\n     7\t   java.net.http client and drives the projection and its own mirror\n     8\t   step over the dialed attachment; its link sends the descriptor\n     9\t   probe and drains inside every operation. Nothing is mocked: bytes\n    10\t   cross a loopback WebSocket in both directions, and the facts are\n    11\t   the plan's slice-3 proof -- the toy end to end; the surface learned\n    12\t   from the probe's answer; both directions serving on one connection;\n    13\t   a closed connection observed as the link's end (2.4).\n    14\t\n    15\t   The test is the composition's cadence: `tick!` advances both ends\n    16\t   one turn, as a driver would, and `settle!` keeps ticking until an\n    17\t   operation stops answering the toy's not-yet outcomes.\"\n    18\t  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is]]\n    19\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    20\t            [dao.stream.remote :as remote]\n    21\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]\n    22\t            [dao.stream.ws :as ws]\n    23\t            [dao.stream.ws.jvm :as jvm]\n    24\t            [dao.stream.ws-project :as project]\n    25\t            [org.httpkit.server :as http]))\n    26\t\n    27\t\n    28\t(def ^:private admission\n    29\t  {:retention :evict-oldest :capacity 64 :value-domain :portable-values})\n    30\t\n    31\t\n    32\t(def ^:private handoff-admission\n    33\t  {:retention :evict-oldest :capacity 1 :value-domain :host-values})\n    34\t\n    35\t\n    36\t(def ^:private path \"/streams/toy\")\n    37\t\n    38\t\n    39\t(defn- buffer\n    40\t  [capacity]\n    41\t  (:dao.stream/handle\n    42\t    (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type ringbuffer/transport-type\n    43\t                         ringbuffer/capacity-key capacity})))\n    44\t\n    45\t\n    46\t(defn- newest\n    47\t  [handle]\n    48\t  (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor handle stream/anchor-newest)))\n    49\t\n    50\t\n    51\t(defn- eventually\n    52\t  \"Poll pred every 10ms until truthy or the deadline; nil on timeout.\"\n    53\t  [pred ms]\n    54\t  (let [deadline (+ (System/currentTimeMillis) ms)]\n    55\t    (loop []\n    56\t      (or (pred)\n    57\t          (when (> deadline (System/currentTimeMillis))\n    58\t            (Thread/sleep 10)\n    59\t            (recur))))))\n    60\t\n    61\t\n    62\t(defn- served-stream\n    63\t  \"The toy's source: the single value, complete history -- the owner's\n    64\t   close is what makes a later read answer the source's own end.\"\n    65\t  [value]\n    66\t  (let [s (buffer 16)]\n    67\t    (stream/append! s value)\n    68\t    (stream/close! s)\n    69\t    s))\n    70\t\n    71\t\n    72\t(defn- toy\n    73\t  \"Both peers of the toy. B: endpoint, acceptor, and a real listener\n    74\t   whose upgrades run ws/accept-connection!; A: a real client\n    75\t   attacher, the projection onto its ring, and its own mirror over\n    76\t   `table` -- A serves \\\"str-2\\\" back over the same kind of\n    77\t   connection.\"\n    78\t  []\n    79\t  (let [str-1 (served-stream \"hello\")\n    80\t        str-2 (served-stream \"backward\")\n    81\t        descriptor {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/ws\n    82\t                    :dao.stream/identity \"str-1\"\n    83\t                    :ws/host \"127.0.0.1\"\n    84\t                    :ws/port 1\n    85\t                    :ws/path path}\n    86\t        offers (buffer 1)\n    87\t        acks (buffer 1)\n    88\t        control (buffer 16)\n    89\t        endpoint (ws/make-endpoint\n    90\t                   {:served {path descriptor}\n    91\t                    :control {:dao.stream/handle control\n    92\t                              :dao.stream/surface #{:writer}}\n    93\t                    :control-admission admission\n    94\t                    :slots [{:offer {:dao.stream/handle offers\n    95\t                                     :dao.stream/surface #{:writer}}\n    96\t                             :offer-admission handoff-admission\n    97\t                             :ack {:dao.stream/handle acks\n    98\t                                   :dao.stream/surface #{:writer}}\n    99\t                             :ack-admission handoff-admission\n   100\t                             :ack-cursor (newest acks)}]\n   101\t                    :expiry-ms nil})\n   102\t        acceptor\n   103\t        (project/make-acceptor\n   104\t          {:endpoint endpoint\n   105\t           :slots [{:offer-reader offers\n   106\t                    :offer-cursor (newest offers)\n   107\t                    :ack-writer {:dao.stream/handle acks\n   108\t                                 :dao.stream/surface #{:writer}}}]\n   109\t           :table {\"str-1\" {:handle str-1 :surface #{:reader}}}\n   110\t           :make-media\n   111\t           (fn [_offer]\n   112\t             (let [traffic (buffer 64)\n   113\t                   channel (buffer 64)]\n   114\t               {:traffic {:dao.stream/handle traffic\n   115\t                          :dao.stream/surface #{:writer}}\n   116\t                :admission admission\n   117\t                :reader traffic\n   118\t                :cursor (newest traffic)\n   119\t                :ring channel}))})\n   120\t        deposits (atom [])\n   121\t        listener\n   122\t        (jvm/listen!\n   123\t          {:bind-host \"127.0.0.1\"\n   124\t           :bind-port 0\n   125\t           :accept!\n   126\t           (fn [target socket now]\n   127\t             (ws/accept-connection! endpoint target socket now))\n   128\t           :deposit!\n   129\t           (fn [kind detail] (swap! deposits conj [kind detail]))})\n   130\t        bound\n   131\t        (eventually #(http/server-port (:ws.jvm/server listener)) 5000)\n   132\t        traffic (buffer 64)\n   133\t        events (buffer 64)\n   134\t        attacher\n   135\t        (ws/make-attacher\n   136\t          {:traffic {:dao.stream/handle traffic\n   137\t                     :dao.stream/surface #{:writer}}\n   138\t           :admission admission\n   139\t           :connect! jvm/connect!})\n   140\t        dial\n   141\t        (project/dial\n   142\t          {:attach! attacher\n   143\t           :traffic {:dao.stream/handle traffic\n   144\t                     :dao.stream/surface #{:writer}}\n   145\t           :cursor (newest traffic)\n   146\t           :ring (buffer 64)\n   147\t           :table {\"str-2\" {:handle str-2 :surface #{:reader}}}\n   148\t           :dao.stream.remote/events events})\n   149\t        values-of\n   150\t        (fn [h]\n   151\t          (loop [c (:dao.stream/cursor\n   152\t                     (stream/cursor h stream/anchor-oldest))\n   153\t                 acc []]\n   154\t            (let [r (stream/next h c)]\n   155\t              (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n   156\t                (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r) (conj acc (:dao.stream/value r)))\n   157\t                (vec acc)))))]\n   158\t    (when (nil? bound)\n   159\t      (jvm/stop-listening! listener (fn []))\n   160\t      (throw (ex-info \"the toy's listener never bound\"\n   161\t                      {:deposits @deposits})))\n   162\t    {:descriptor (assoc descriptor :ws/port bound)\n   163\t     :acceptor acceptor\n   164\t     :listener listener\n   165\t     :dial dial\n   166\t     :events events\n   167\t     :values-of values-of}))\n   168\t\n   169\t\n   170\t(defn- reflect!\n   171\t  \"A's attach! on a remote descriptor naming `identity` over the toy's\n   172\t   channel.\"\n   173\t  [toy identity]\n   174\t  (project/dial-attach! (:dial toy)\n   175\t                        {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/remote\n   176\t                         :dao.stream/identity identity\n   177\t                         :dao.stream/channel (:descriptor toy)}))\n   178\t\n   179\t\n   180\t(defn- tick!\n   181\t  \"One cadence turn of the whole toy: B's accepting composition, then\n   182\t   A's dialing composition.\"\n   183\t  [toy]\n   184\t  (project/accept-step! (:acceptor toy) (System/currentTimeMillis))\n   185\t  (project/dial-step! (:dial toy)))\n   186\t\n   187\t\n   188\t(defn- drive!\n   189\t  \"Tick the toy until `pred` holds or the deadline passes; true when\n   190\t   it held.\"\n   191\t  [toy pred ms]\n   192\t  (let [deadline (+ (System/currentTimeMillis) ms)]\n   193\t    (loop []\n   194\t      (or (pred)\n   195\t          (when (< (System/currentTimeMillis) deadline)\n   196\t            (tick! toy)\n   197\t            (Thread/sleep 10)\n   198\t            (recur))))))\n   199\t\n   200\t\n   201\t(defn- settle!\n   202\t  \"Apply `op`, ticking the toy between attempts, until it stops\n   203\t   answering the toy's not-yet outcomes -- the pre-answer\n   204\t   transport-error retry and blocked -- or the deadline passes.\"\n   205\t  [toy op ms]\n   206\t  (let [deadline (+ (System/currentTimeMillis) ms)]\n   207\t    (loop [r (op)]\n   208\t      (if (and (contains? #{:dao.stream/transport-error\n   209\t                            :dao.stream/blocked}\n   210\t                          (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n   211\t               (< (System/currentTimeMillis) deadline))\n   212\t        (do (tick! toy)\n   213\t            (Thread/sleep 10)\n   214\t            (recur (op)))\n   215\t        r))))\n   216\t\n   217\t\n   218\t(defn- b-reflect!\n   219\t  \"B's own reflection of `identity` over the accepted connection: the\n   220\t   session end this side holds, through the remote attacher.\"\n   221\t  [toy identity]\n   222\t  (let [attachment (first (keys (project/sessions (:acceptor toy))))\n   223\t        end (project/session-end (:acceptor toy) attachment)\n   224\t        result ((remote/attacher\n   225\t                  {:dao.stream.remote/channels {(:descriptor toy) end}})\n   226\t                {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/remote\n   227\t                 :dao.stream/identity identity\n   228\t                 :dao.stream/channel (:descriptor toy)})]\n   229\t    result))\n   230\t\n   231\t\n   232\t(deftest the-toy-crosses-a-real-socket\n   233\t  (let [toy (toy)\n   234\t        attached (reflect! toy \"str-1\")\n   235\t        refl (:dao.stream/handle attached)]\n   236\t    (try\n   237\t      (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome attached)))\n   238\t      (is (string? (:dao.stream/attachment attached)))\n   239\t      (is (drive! toy #(seq (project/sessions (:acceptor toy))) 5000)\n   240\t          \"B adopted the connection and acknowledged its offer\")\n   241\t      ;; descriptor is local: ok before any confirmation (2.4).\n   242\t      (let [d (stream/descriptor refl)]\n   243\t        (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome d)))\n   244\t        (is (= \"str-1\" (:dao.stream/identity d))))\n   245\t      ;; cursor :oldest: the link sends, answers the retry, then the\n   246\t      ;; next ask files the source's ok.\n   247\t      (let [r (settle! toy #(stream/cursor refl stream/anchor-oldest)\n   248\t                       5000)]\n   249\t        (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r)))\n   250\t        (is (some? (:dao.stream/cursor r)))\n   251\t        (is (= #{:reader} (:dao.stream.remote/surface\n   252\t                            (first ((:values-of toy) (:events toy)))))\n   253\t            \"the probe's answer crossed the wire: the link's event\n   254\t             writer recorded the confirmation carrying the served\n   255\t             stream's declared surface\")\n   256\t        ;; next c0: blocked, then the source's own ok \"hello\" c1.\n   257\t        (let [c0 (:dao.stream/cursor r)\n   258\t              n (settle! toy #(stream/next refl c0) 5000)]\n   259\t          (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome n)))\n   260\t          (is (= \"hello\" (:dao.stream/value n))\n   261\t              \"nothing knew it was a string\")\n   262\t          ;; next c1: the source's own end.\n   263\t          (let [e (settle! toy\n   264\t                           #(stream/next refl (:dao.stream/cursor n))\n   265\t                           5000)]\n   266\t            (is (= :dao.stream/end (:dao.stream/outcome e))))))\n   267\t      (finally\n   268\t        (jvm/stop-listening! (:listener toy) (fn []))))))\n   269\t\n   270\t\n   271\t(deftest both-directions-serve-on-one-connection\n   272\t  (let [toy (toy)\n   273\t        a-refl (:dao.stream/handle (reflect! toy \"str-1\"))]\n   274\t    (try\n   275\t      (is (drive! toy #(seq (project/sessions (:acceptor toy))) 5000))\n   276\t      (is (= :dao.stream/ok\n   277\t             (:dao.stream/outcome\n   278\t               (settle! toy\n   279\t                        #(stream/cursor a-refl stream/anchor-oldest)\n   280\t                        5000)))\n   281\t          \"A's direction established\")\n   282\t      (let [b-attached (b-reflect! toy \"str-2\")\n   283\t            b-refl (:dao.stream/handle b-attached)]\n   284\t        (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome b-attached))\n   285\t            \"B attached a reflection over the same accepted connection\")\n   286\t        (let [r (settle! toy\n   287\t                         #(stream/cursor b-refl stream/anchor-oldest)\n   288\t                         5000)]\n   289\t          (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r)))\n   290\t          (let [n (settle! toy\n   291\t                           #(stream/next b-refl (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   292\t                           5000)]\n   293\t            (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome n)))\n   294\t            (is (= \"backward\" (:dao.stream/value n))\n   295\t                \"B read A's stream back over the one connection: the\n   296\t                 wire stayed symmetric, one request and one answer at\n   297\t                 a time, each end serving its own table\"))))\n   298\t      (finally\n   299\t        (jvm/stop-listening! (:listener toy) (fn []))))))\n   300\t\n   301\t\n   302\t(deftest a-closed-connection-is-the-links-end\n   303\t  (let [toy (toy)\n   304\t        a-refl (:dao.stream/handle (reflect! toy \"str-1\"))]\n   305\t    (try\n   306\t      (is (drive! toy #(seq (project/sessions (:acceptor toy))) 5000))\n   307\t      (let [a-c0 (:dao.stream/cursor\n   308\t                   (settle! toy\n   309\t                            #(stream/cursor a-refl stream/anchor-oldest)\n   310\t                            5000))\n   311\t            b-attached (b-reflect! toy \"str-2\")\n   312\t            b-refl (:dao.stream/handle b-attached)\n   313\t            b-c0 (:dao.stream/cursor\n   314\t                   (settle! toy\n   315\t                            #(stream/cursor b-refl stream/anchor-oldest)\n   316\t                            5000))]\n   317\t        (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome b-attached)))\n   318\t        ;; A detaches.  Each endpoint deposits its one terminal event,\n   319\t        ;; each projection closes its ring.\n   320\t        (stream/close! (:handle (project/channel (:dial toy))))\n   321\t        (is (drive! toy\n   322\t                    #(let [a-project (:project (project/channel\n   323\t                                                 (:dial toy)))\n   324\t                           b-session (first (vals (project/sessions\n   325\t                                                    (:acceptor toy))))]\n   326\t                       (and (project/closed? a-project)\n   327\t                            (some? b-session)\n   328\t                            (project/closed? (:project b-session))))\n   329\t                    5000)\n   330\t            \"both ends saw the terminal event and both rings closed\")\n   331\t        ;; Each link observes the channel's end: not a retry.\n   332\t        (let [r (stream/next a-refl a-c0)]\n   333\t          (is (= :dao.stream/transport-error (:dao.stream/outcome r)))\n   334\t          (is (= :dao.stream.remote/channel-gone\n   335\t                 (:dao.stream.remote/reason r))\n   336\t              \"A's link abandoned the channel (2.4)\"))\n   337\t        (let [r (stream/next b-refl b-c0)]\n   338\t          (is (= :dao.stream/transport-error (:dao.stream/outcome r)))\n   339\t          (is (= :dao.stream.remote/channel-gone\n   340\t                 (:dao.stream.remote/reason r))\n   341\t              \"B's link abandoned the channel too: the one connection\n   342\t               carried both directions\"))\n   343\t        ;; The name outlives the channel: descriptor still answers ok.\n   344\t        (is (= :dao.stream/ok\n   345\t               (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/descriptor a-refl)))))\n   346\t      (finally\n   347\t        (jvm/stop-listening! (:listener toy) (fn []))))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
