{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md | sed -n '314,352p'; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/ws_project.cljc | sed -n '325,385p'; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc | sed -n '570,610p'; rg -n 'defn mirror-step|:dao.stream/gap|defn attacher' src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"   314\t\n   315\tA channel declares a portable value domain, a frame budget, and whether it\n   316\tis ordered and reliable; the link reads the last as composition data for\n   317\t`:dao.stream.remote/resend-after`, and nothing else in section 2 changes\n   318\tper channel.\n   319\t\n   320\t### 3.1 WebSocket\n   321\t\n   322\t`dao.stream.ws` as specified in `dao.stream.ws.md` is the socket layer, and\n   323\ta channel is one of its attachments plus a projection. **Reused**: the\n   324\tattachment model and identity; the adapter that deposits every event as\n   325\t`{:ws/attachment id :ws/event e :ws/value v}` on the medium the composition\n   326\twired; the writer handle, whose `append!` frames each value as one\n   327\t`{:ws/frame :ws/value :ws/value v}` message in the negotiated codec profile\n   328\t(Transit-JSON text or the CBOR binary profile); the bounded acceptance\n   329\thandoff with slot and acknowledgement; the resolution and lifecycle\n   330\tvocabulary. Ordered and reliable; frame budget unbounded.\n   331\t\n   332\t**New, the projection.** The mirror and the link speak raw request and\n   333\tanswer maps, so each channel end composes one step, `ws-project`, between\n   334\tthe ws deposit medium and the channel. The channel reader is a ring buffer\n   335\tthe composition wires; the channel writer is the ws handle itself.\n   336\t`ws-project` holds the reading cursor on the attachment's traffic medium,\n   337\tkeeps the events whose `:ws/attachment` names this channel, appends the\n   338\t`:ws/value` of each `:ws/payload` onto the ring buffer, and drops\n   339\t`:ws/error` diagnostics. A terminal lifecycle event for the attachment\n   340\t(`:ws/closed`, `:ws/ended`) or a failure resolution (`:ws/not-found`,\n   341\t`:ws/transport-error`) makes `ws-project` close the ring buffer: channel\n   342\tloss is then the link's `end` observation (2.4). `ws-project` is a step the\n   343\tcomposition drives at its own cadence, as it drives `endpoint-step`.\n   344\t\n   345\tDirection is establishment, not authority. A WebSocket has a dialer and an\n   346\tacceptor because TCP does. Once established the channel is symmetric and\n   347\tnothing in this document remembers who dialed. Hosts: clj, cljs on Node and\n   348\tcljd may dial or accept (`src/clj/dao/stream/ws/jvm.clj`,\n   349\t`src/cljs/dao/stream/ws/node.cljs`, `src/cljd/dao/stream/ws/dart.cljd`);\n   350\tcljs in a browser may only dial (`src/cljs/dao/stream/ws/browser.cljs`).\n   351\t\n   352\t### 3.2 UDP\n   325\t(defn dial-attach!\n   326\t  \"Attach one reflection of `descriptor` (a :dao.stream/remote\n   327\t   descriptor) through the dialed channel: the ws attach runs first,\n   328\t   the attachment's projection is composed, and the remote attacher\n   329\t   answers with the reflection -- its confirmation deferred, per\n   330\t   dao.stream.remote.md 2.4, to the descriptor probe the link sends\n   331\t   now. A channel attach that fails answers the ws attacher's own\n   332\t   outcome. Returns the remote attach! result.\"\n   333\t  [dial descriptor]\n   334\t  (let [{:keys [attach! traffic cursor ring channel policy]} @dial\n   335\t        r (attach! (:dao.stream/channel descriptor))]\n   336\t    (if-not (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n   337\t      r\n   338\t      (let [cd (:dao.stream/channel descriptor)\n   339\t            handle (:dao.stream/handle r)\n   340\t            project (projection {:attachment (:dao.stream/attachment r)\n   341\t                                 :traffic (:dao.stream/handle traffic)\n   342\t                                 :cursor cursor\n   343\t                                 :ring ring})\n   344\t            reflect! (remote/attacher\n   345\t                       (merge policy\n   346\t                              {:dao.stream.remote/channels\n   347\t                               {cd {:reader ring :writer handle}}}))]\n   348\t        (reset! channel {:attachment (:dao.stream/attachment r)\n   349\t                         :handle handle :project project})\n   350\t        (reflect! descriptor)))))\n   351\t\n   352\t\n   353\t(defn dial-step!\n   354\t  \"Drive the dialing composition one tick, at the composition's\n   355\t   cadence: the attachment's projection first, so what the wire\n   356\t   deposited reaches the ring, then this end's own mirror step over\n   357\t   the projected reader and the socket handle, answering the other\n   358\t   direction's requests against this end's table. Returns the\n   359\t   mirror's advanced reading cursor.\"\n   360\t  [dial]\n   361\t  (let [{:keys [ring table channel mirror-cursor]} @dial]\n   362\t    (when-some [project (:project @channel)]\n   363\t      (step! project))\n   364\t    (when-some [handle (:handle @channel)]\n   365\t      (swap! mirror-cursor\n   366\t             (fn [c] (remote/mirror-step table ring c handle))))\n   367\t    @mirror-cursor))\n   368\t\n   369\t\n   370\t(defn channel\n   371\t  \"The dialed channel as data: {:attachment id :handle h :project p} --\n   372\t   the ws attachment identity, the ws handle (the channel writer), and\n   373\t   the attachment's projection. Nil before the first dial-attach!. A\n   374\t   composition that owns the connection's lifetime closes the handle\n   375\t   here.\"\n   376\t  [dial]\n   377\t  @(:channel @dial))\n   570\t      (release-slot! endpoint index (:attachment slot)))))\n   571\t\n   572\t\n   573\t(defn endpoint-step\n   574\t  \"Poll each configured acknowledgement slot once, without waiting or\n   575\t   self-scheduling.  Returns the endpoint after retaining its next cursors.\"\n   576\t  [endpoint now]\n   577\t  ;; A pending connection can be lost before any acknowledgement: the peer\n   578\t  ;; closes, the wire protocol fails, or its own handle is closed.  Each of\n   579\t  ;; those paths closes the handle's state and deposits its terminal event;\n   580\t  ;; this is where the endpoint observes that and returns the slot, so bounded\n   581\t  ;; admission is a live bound rather than a monotonically shrinking one.\n   582\t  (doseq [[index slot] (map-indexed vector (:slots (endpoint-state endpoint)))\n   583\t          :when (and (= :pending (:status slot))\n   584\t                     (= :closed (:phase @(:handle-state slot))))]\n   585\t    (release-slot! endpoint index (:attachment slot)))\n   586\t  (doseq [[index slot] (map-indexed vector (:slots (endpoint-state endpoint)))\n   587\t          :when (= :pending (:status slot))]\n   588\t    (let [next (stream/next (:dao.stream/handle (:ack slot)) (:ack-cursor slot))]\n   589\t      (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome next))\n   590\t        (swap! (:state endpoint) assoc-in [:slots index :ack-cursor] (:dao.stream/cursor next))\n   591\t        (let [ack (:dao.stream/value next)]\n   592\t          (cond\n   593\t            (not= (:attachment slot) (:ws/attachment ack)) nil\n   594\t            (valid-ack? ack (:attachment slot)) (accept-slot! endpoint index slot ack)\n   595\t            :else (let [hstate (:handle-state slot)]\n   596\t                    (swap! hstate assoc :phase :closed)\n   597\t                    (invoke-close! (:socket @hstate) protocol-close-code \"dao.stream/invalid-ack\")\n   598\t                    (terminal! hstate (:attachment slot) :ws/closed)\n   599\t                    (release-slot! endpoint index (:attachment slot))))))))\n   600\t  ;; Expiry is deliberately clock-domain explicit.  An endpoint composition\n   601\t  ;; may set `:opened-at` when it accepts an offer; this transport does not\n   602\t  ;; invent wall-clock time or a scheduler.\n   603\t  (when-let [expiry (:expiry-ms (:config endpoint))]\n   604\t    (doseq [[index slot] (map-indexed vector (:slots (endpoint-state endpoint)))\n   605\t            :when (and (= :pending (:status slot)) (:opened-at slot)\n   606\t                       (<= (+ (:opened-at slot) expiry) now))]\n   607\t      (let [hstate (:handle-state slot)]\n   608\t        (swap! hstate assoc :phase :closed)\n   609\t        (invoke-close! (:socket @hstate) 1000 \"dao.stream/acceptance-expired\")\n   610\t        (terminal! hstate (:attachment slot) :ws/closed)\n185:(defn mirror-step\n209:          :dao.stream/gap (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n491:          :dao.stream/gap\n734:(defn attacher\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
